    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d144">

                <pb facs="0190" n="180" xml:id="pg180"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">548.G1/121: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Standley</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-05-15T13:00:00+03:00">May 15, 1943—1
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received May 15—11:56 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>457. Department’s 230, May 10, 7 p.m., to Kuibyshev. Please clarify what is meant
                    by the separate declaration “similar to the Polish”.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Standley</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
